    skos:prefLabel 'gas chromatography-reduction gas detection'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A technique to separate gases, volatile substances or substances dissolved in a volatile solvent by transport by an inert gas through a column packed with a sorbent. The separated components are then analysed by a detector that measures the concentration of a target gas by reducing it at an electrode and measuring the resulting current.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S04::S041064'^^xsd:string .
